The system design (2026-09-22-canlin-system-design.md, §2) says: "The i686 test suite runs under qemu-system-i386 -cpu pentium2 -m 1024 because the host silently executes SSE." That is the full-system harness and it needs a canlin-os image (canlin-os k2, still open). Since 2026-11-15 the suites also run under the user-mode emulator: the musl cross toolchain is at ~/opt/i686-linux-musl-cross, `make TARGET=i686` builds with -march=i686 -mno-sse -static, and the binaries run under `qemu-i386 -cpu pentium2` - a program with movaps dies there with signal 4, so the profile really has no SSE. The spec should say what each of the two gates proves and that the user-mode one is the interim until the image exists. The same goes for the build spine: the target needs a RUNNER hook (k143), otherwise the gate is a hand-typed command.

Specs updated (docs only, no code touched). System design §2 now names the two i686 gates and what each proves: the user-mode gate `qemu-i386 -cpu pentium2 ./build/i686/t/<suite>` (in use since 2026-11-15; instruction compatibility on a Pentium II profile — a program with movaps dies there with signal 4 while plain qemu-i386 runs it) and the full-system gate `qemu-system-i386 -cpu pentium2 -m 1024` with a canlin-os image (system operation: kernel, drivers, framebuffer, boot). The user-mode gate is named as the interim gate; the canlin-os image does not exist yet (canlin-os board, ticket k2, still backlog — its own card says 'Until then canlin has only qemu-i386 user-mode evidence'), and the two are never reported as one QEMU result. §2 also names the musl cross toolchain and the -march=i686 -mno-sse -static build. System design §12 (Testing) follows: portable suites run on host + user-mode QEMU, the full-system P2-QEMU run waits for the image, the i686 suites have no runner hook yet so the gate is started by hand, the machine-readable result comes with the canlin-os harness. http-transport §9 (Gates) and libs §8 (Verification of a lib) now name the user-mode gate in their gate lists and point at system design §2; the http-transport handshake-time number on P2-QEMU is marked as waiting for the canlin-os image. Status line records the 2026-11-15 amendment.

